              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mary has a standard deck of 52 cards and a six-sided die. She draws a card and then rolls the die. What is the probability that the number on the die matches the number on the card?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p24-q9-ace-convention",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Treat an ace as 1.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{13}$",
      "worked": "The matching card values are ace, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6. Each has four cards, and the six matching cases have equal probability.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{match})&=6\\times\\frac{4}{52}\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\\\P(\\text{match})&=\\frac{1}{13}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
